#
# \brief  Sponge OS provider-stall isolation scenario (P3.1 red scenario)
# \author Sponge OS contributors
# \date   2026-10-28
#
# Phase 16 runtime-overhaul task P3.1 (docs/plans/phase16-runtime-overhaul.md),
# failure domain FD4 / decision D16R.8. RED receipt first (D16R.16): on
# today's shared vfs_var this scenario FAILS at its per-path gates; the
# P3.2 vfs_pkg/vfs_log split flips it green.
#
# ========================================================================
# What is under test
# ========================================================================
#
# The product's P4 (SPONGE-VAR) File_system provider is ONE `vfs`
# instance, `vfs_var`, carrying BOTH P4 session regions (the P0.5 audit,
# docs/evidence/phase16-runtime-patch-io-audit.md §3.1):
#
#   policy region /pkgd — the package store (sponge_pkgd's <vfs> store
#                         mount, the "other P4 consumer")
#   policy region /log  — the log sink (sponge_logdisk's <vfs> mount,
#                         label_prefix: sponge_logdisk ->)
#
# One instance = one entrypoint, one rump ext2 mount, one Block session
# to part_block/P4. Whatever stalls that instance stalls BOTH consumers
# (the shared-fate property this scenario demonstrates). P3.2 splits the
# wiring into two instances on the same partition (vfs_pkg / vfs_log);
# then a log-path stall stays on vfs_log and the store survives.
#
# ========================================================================
# The injected fault: a deterministic SOFTWARE provider stall
# ========================================================================
#
# The P4 provider's Block route points at 'blk_stall' — a test/ep_wedge
# in its default mode ("logs one line and blocks its entrypoint
# forever"). It never announces any service, so init queues every Block
# session request aimed at it forever. The vfs instance's rump ext2
# mount opens its Block session at construct and therefore parks in
# construct: the provider NEVER announces File_system, and every P4
# session create queues at init indefinitely. That is the stall.
#
# This is SOFTWARE, not media:
#   * the injection is a start-node route line plus ep_wedge's own
#     "ep_wedge: alive — entrypoint wedging now" marker — deterministic,
#     greppable, and absent on a healthy boot;
#   * the QEMU disk is never touched. The SAME disk keeps serving P3
#     throughout the stall — part_block still enumerates the GPT
#     (test/partition_check reuses its byte assertion "Number: 3") and
#     the rom_sys chain (cached_fs_rom -> vfs_sys -> part_block/P3)
#     still serves a marker ROM DURING the stall window. A physical
#     USB/media death would take those down too; the scenario asserts
#     they stay up and prints
#       provider-stall-control: PASS — ... software provider stall —
#       NOT a physical media/USB failure
#     so the receipt can never be mistaken for a media-failure test.
#
# The affected consumer (the log sink, sponge_logdisk) degrades
# VISIBLY: its File_system create is parked inside its constructor, so
# its healthy markers ("sponge_logdisk: logging to ..." and the
# tick_log tick lines) never appear. The scenario asserts their absence
# (bounded, host-side) and prints an explicit
#   provider-stall: path=log-sink DEGRADED (expected ...)
# marker.
#
# ========================================================================
# Positive control (the fault detector must demonstrably fire)
# ========================================================================
#
# An "isolation" claim is void if the fault never landed or the
# detector is blind. Before any isolation verdict the scenario asserts,
# and fails loudly otherwise:
#   (1) the injection fired       — 'ep_wedge: alive' present;
#   (2) the log consumer degraded — no 'sponge_logdisk: logging to',
#                                   no 'tick alive' within the window;
#   (3) the container is alive    — the liveness bystander (ep_wedge
#                                   liveness_ms mode) keeps printing
#                                   'bystander: alive t=' through the
#                                   stall (no entrypoint/global park);
#   (4) the media is alive        — 'partition-check: PASS' (part_block
#                                   GPT enumeration on the same disk).
# These print 'provider-stall-control: PASS/FAIL'.
#
# ========================================================================
# Per-path assertions (explicit per-path RED markers)
# ========================================================================
#
#   path=sys-rom    PASS/RED  — ROM 'sys_marker' read via the rom_sys
#                               chain during the stall (unrelated ROM +
#                               media-alive evidence).
#   path=pkgd-store PASS/RED  — write + read back /pkgd/store/pstall.txt
#                               through the P4 store region, BOUNDED.
#                               Today (shared vfs_var) the create rides
#                               the stalled instance and parks: RED,
#                               'reason=create_parked_30000ms'. After
#                               the split: PASS.
#   path=log-sink   DEGRADED  — asserted host-side (see above). No probe
#                               can reach that policy: only a child
#                               literally named 'sponge_logdisk' matches
#                               the 'sponge_logdisk -> ' label_prefix.
#
# Markers are printed by repos/sponge/src/test/provider_isolation_probe
# (per path: 'provider-isolation-probe: PASS path=...' or
# 'provider-isolation-probe: RED path=... reason=...') and by this
# script ('provider-stall: path=...'). Every wait is bounded: the probe
# bounds its workers at 30 s and always prints its verdict; every
# run_genode_until below carries a finite timeout.
#
# Expected RED receipt (today, shared vfs_var):
#   provider-stall-control: PASS
#   provider-isolation-probe: PASS path=sys-rom
#   provider-isolation-probe: RED path=pkgd-store reason=create_parked_30000ms
#   provider-stall: path=pkgd-store RED (shared vfs_var fate ...)
#   -> error exit; 'provider-isolation-probe: PASS' absent.
#
# ========================================================================
# P3.2 flip guide (the commit that turns this scenario green)
# ========================================================================
#
# Split the 'vfs_var' start node below into TWO instances on partition 4
# (same binary, same lib routes; no new partitions — D16R.2):
#
#   vfs_pkg: config = '+ vfs | + rump ...' +
#            '+ default-policy | root: /pkgd | writeable: yes'
#            Block route: '+ service Block | + child part_block'
#            (part_block gains '+ policy | label_prefix: vfs_pkg |
#             partition: 4 | writeable: yes' next to vfs_sys's P3 row)
#   vfs_log: config = '+ vfs | + rump ...' +
#            '+ policy | label_prefix: sponge_logdisk -> | root: /log |
#             writeable: yes'
#            Block route: '+ service Block | + child blk_stall'
#            (THE STALL STAYS ON THE LOG PATH — that is the point.)
#
#   Then re-aim the consumers: the probe's File_system route to
#   '+ child vfs_pkg', sponge_logdisk's to '+ child vfs_log', and the
#   part_block 'vfs_var' policy row to 'vfs_pkg'.
#
#   Expected result: 'provider-isolation-probe: PASS' (store round-trip
#   works AND is corroborated on media by e2cp read-back), while the log
#   sink still degrades visibly — the isolated-fate property of
#   D16R.8/FD4.
#
# ========================================================================
# Conventions and known gotchas applied (docs/08-development.md §4,
# docs/evidence/logdisk-field-diagnosis.md §5)
# ========================================================================
#
#   * lib/ld in the build list; build_boot_image $boot_modules with the
#     vfs/rump chain libs listed explicitly (transitive deps of
#     lib/vfs_rump are not build artifacts — run/sponge-boot.run idiom).
#   * image/iso is dropped from the include list: power_on/qemu prefers
#     a stale ISO over the disk image (logdisk §5.1) and this scenario's
#     assertions are about the DISK chain.
#   * No run_power_cycle before the boot (logdisk §5.2) — single boot.
#   * tool/mkdata is NOT invoked from tclsh (its Mojo launcher dies
#     under tclsh exec — logdisk §5.4, also breaks sponge-persist-disk
#     in this environment): the docs/14 §4.3 P4 sequence is spelled out
#     inline below, same steps.
#   * mke2fs's exit status is not the success signal (logdisk §5.3):
#     the e2mkdir that follows it is.
#   * /pkgd, /pkgd/store and /log are pre-created on P4: vfs resolves a
#     session root at create time (logdisk §3(c)).
#   * Component LOG deliberately stays on core/serial — nothing routes
#     LOG to the sink here. The LOG-bootstrapping coupling (logdisk §4)
#     is a separate failure mode that P3.2 does not address; mixing it
#     into this scenario would make the P3.2 flip ambiguous.
#   * GUI sessions are not asserted: this is the minimal headless slice
#     (headless like run/sponge-persist-disk.run). The plan P3.1
#     parenthetical mentions GUI; that stays with the full product
#     scenarios.
#
# Build + run:
#   make -C genode/build/x86_64 run/sponge-provider-stall \
#       KERNEL=sel4 BOARD=pc RUN_OPT="--include image/disk"
#
# SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
#

assert {[have_spec sel4]} \
	"sponge-provider-stall requires KERNEL=sel4 (BOARD=pc)."

##
# Ensure essential run-framework plugins are loaded (a command-line
# RUN_OPT override discards build.conf's accumulated --include lines).
#
proc ensure_plugin_loaded { name } {
	if {![have_include $name]} {
		set path [genode_dir]/tool/run/$name
		puts "sourcing $path (missing from RUN_OPT, restored by run script)"
		source $path
		global include_list
		lappend include_list $name
	}
}

ensure_plugin_loaded boot_dir/sel4
ensure_plugin_loaded power_on/qemu
ensure_plugin_loaded log/qemu

#
# logdisk-field-diagnosis §5.1: a stale image/iso in the include list
# silently beats the disk image (power_on/qemu prefers the ISO, and the
# ISO is only rebuilt when the run directory changes). This scenario is
# a disk-chain scenario — drop image/iso unconditionally.
#
global include_list
set include_list [lsearch -all -inline -not -exact $include_list "image/iso"]

#
# P4 (SPONGE-VAR) data-area size. The product's SPONGE-VAR is 64 MiB
# (docs/evidence/logdisk-field-diagnosis.md §2) — same here, so the
# ext2/rump behaviour matches the media.
#
set data_mib 64

#
# Build — Tier-0 storage chain (run/sponge-persist-disk.run's shape)
# plus the shared-provider wiring under test: rom_sys (unrelated system
# ROM), sponge_logdisk (log-path consumer) and the probes.
#
set build_components {
	core lib/ld init timer
	server/report_rom
	driver/platform driver/acpi app/pci_decode
	driver/ahci
	server/part_block server/vfs server/cached_fs_rom
	lib/vfs lib/vfs_rump
	sponge_logdisk
	test/provider_isolation_probe test/partition_check test/ep_wedge
}

build $build_components

create_boot_directory

#
# On base-sel4 every boot module must land in bin/ BEFORE
# build_boot_image (sponge-persist-disk idiom).
#
exec mkdir -p bin

#
# Stage the sys-rom marker at [run_dir]/system/sys_marker — image/disk
# copies the run directory into P3's ext2, so it lands at
# /system/sys_marker, served by rom_sys (cached_fs_rom root /system).
# The probe byte-compares against the same literal.
#
exec mkdir -p [run_dir]/system
set marker_fh [open "[run_dir]/system/sys_marker" w]
fconfigure $marker_fh -translation binary
puts -nonewline $marker_fh "sponge-provider-stall sys-rom marker\n"
close $marker_fh

# ========================================================================
# init configuration (Tier 0, HID)
# ========================================================================

install_config {
config
+ parent-provides
  + service ROM
  + service IRQ
  + service IO_MEM
  + service IO_PORT
  + service PD
  + service RM
  + service CPU
  + service LOG

+ default-route
  + any-service
    + parent
    + any-child
+ default | caps: 100 | ram: 1M

+ start timer
  + provides | + service Timer

+ start report_rom | ram: 4M
  + provides
    + service Report
    + service ROM
  + config | verbose: no
    #
    # Storage-chain inter-driver routing (sponge-boot.run /
    # sponge-persist-disk.run): acpi reports the pci table pci_decode
    # reads; pci_decode reports the device tree platform reads. Without
    # these the storage chain never comes up.
    #
    + policy | label: pci_decode -> system | report: acpi -> acpi
    + policy | label: platform -> devices  | report: pci_decode -> devices
    #
    # part_block's partitions report, read by test/partition_check
    # (run/sponge-desktop-disk-nvme.run Tier-0 idiom). The label is the
    # requesting child's name + ROM label.
    #
    + policy | label: partition_check -> partitions | report: part_block -> partitions

+ start acpi | caps: 350 | ram: 4M
  + route
    + service ROM | label_last: ld.lib.so | + parent
    + service Report | + child report_rom
    + service IO_MEM | + parent
    + service LOG | + parent
    + service PD | + parent
    + service RM | + parent
    + service CPU | + parent
    + service ROM | + parent

+ start pci_decode | caps: 350 | ram: 2M
  + route
    + service ROM | label_last: ld.lib.so | + parent
    + service Report | + child report_rom
    + service ROM | label: system | + child report_rom
    + service IO_MEM | + parent
    + service LOG | + parent
    + service PD | + parent
    + service RM | + parent
    + service CPU | + parent
    + service ROM | + parent

+ start platform | caps: 200 | ram: 3M | managing_system: yes
  + provides
    + service Platform
    + service Dma
  + route
    + service ROM | label_last: ld.lib.so | + parent
    + service ROM | label: devices | + child report_rom
    + service Report | + child report_rom
    + service Timer | + child timer
    + service IRQ | + parent
    + service IO_MEM | + parent
    + service IO_PORT | + parent
    + service ROM | + parent
    + service PD | + parent
    + service CPU | + parent
    + service LOG | + parent
  + config
    + report | devices: yes
    + policy | label_prefix: ahci | + pci | class: AHCI

#
# ahci -> Block. The QEMU q35 machine auto-attaches image/disk's
# -drive format=raw,file=<img> to the ICH9 SATA controller (docs/14 §11
# risk 1: ram 128M / caps 5000 for the DMA-able pool).
#
+ start ahci | caps: 5000 | ram: 128M
  + provides | + service Block
  + config
    + report | ports: yes
    + policy | label_prefix: part_block | device: 0 | writeable: yes
  + route
    + service ROM | label_last: ld.lib.so | + parent
    + service Platform | + child platform
    + service Dma | + child platform
    + service Timer | + child timer
    + service Report | + child report_rom
    + service ROM | + parent
    + service PD | + parent
    + service CPU | + parent
    + service LOG | + parent

#
# part_block: partitions pinned BY NUMBER (docs/14 §4.4, the W4
# contract) — P3 GENODE (system ROM chain) and P4 SPONGE-VAR (the
# shared provider under test). The partitions report is enabled for
# test/partition_check (the media-alive witness). The Report route must
# be explicit BEFORE any-service or the report cascades to parent and
# part_block stops (sponge-desktop-disk-nvme.run's note).
#
+ start part_block | caps: 200 | ram: 8M
  + provides | + service Block
  + config
    + report | partitions: yes
    + policy | label_prefix: vfs_sys | partition: 3 | writeable: no
    + policy | label_prefix: vfs_var | partition: 4 | writeable: yes
  + route
    + service ROM | label_last: ld.lib.so | + parent
    + service Block | + child ahci
    + service Report | + child report_rom
    + any-service
      + parent
      + any-child

#
# blk_stall — THE INJECTED FAULT (software provider stall).
#
# test/ep_wedge in its default mode: it logs one line and blocks its
# entrypoint forever. It announces NO service, so init queues every
# session request routed to it indefinitely. The P4 provider's Block
# route below points here, which parks the provider's rump ext2 mount
# at construct — the provider never announces File_system.
#
# P3.2 note: this node stays as the LOG path's Block source after the
# split (see the header's flip guide) — the stall is always aimed at
# "the provider instance serving the log path".
#
+ start blk_stall | caps: 100 | ram: 4M
  + binary | name: ep_wedge
  + provides | + service Block
  + config

#
# bystander — the liveness oracle (ep_wedge liveness_ms mode): prints
# "bystander: alive t=" every second and never blocks. Its continued
# output is the container-alive half of the positive control.
#
+ start bystander | caps: 100 | ram: 4M
  + binary | name: ep_wedge
  + config | liveness_ms: 1000

#
# vfs_sys — the UNRELATED system ROM chain (partition P3): read-only
# rump ext2 over part_block/P3, chroot /system for rom_sys.
#
+ start vfs_sys | caps: 2000 | ram: 32M
  + binary vfs
  + provides | + service File_system
  + config
    + vfs
      + rump | fs: ext2fs | ram: 16M | writeable: no
    + policy | label_prefix: rom_sys | root: /system | writeable: no
  + route
    + service ROM | label_last: ld.lib.so       | + parent
    + service ROM | label_last: vfs.lib.so      | + parent
    + service ROM | label_last: vfs_rump.lib.so | + parent
    + service ROM | label_last: rump.lib.so     | + parent
    + service ROM | label_last: rump_fs.lib.so  | + parent
    + service Block | + child part_block
    + any-service
      + parent
      + any-child

+ start rom_sys | caps: 200 | ram: 16M
  + binary cached_fs_rom
  + provides | + service ROM
  + route
    + service File_system | + child vfs_sys
    + service ROM | label_last: ld.lib.so | + parent
    + any-service
      + parent
      + any-child

#
# vfs_var — THE WIRING UNDER TEST (today's shared P4 provider,
# mirroring the product's run/sponge-desktop-disk-uefi-usb.run:1566 and
# the P0.5 audit §3.1): ONE vfs instance over part_block/P4 carrying
# BOTH session regions:
#
#   default-policy root /pkgd   — the package-store region
#   label_prefix: sponge_logdisk -> root /log — the log-sink region
#
# The catch-all is spelled 'default-policy' (the upstream catch-all
# idiom, genode/repos/os/run/vfs_xoroshiro.run) so the healthy-state
# store check can actually pass: vfs policy matching scores
# label-bearing policies over label-less ones (os/include/os/
# session_policy.h), and a 'default-policy' node is the spelling that
# serves unmatched labels.
#
# Block route -> blk_stall: THE FAULT. With both regions on this one
# instance, stalling it stalls the store path too — the shared fate
# that makes this scenario RED today. P3.2 splits this node per the
# header's flip guide and keeps blk_stall on vfs_log only.
#
+ start vfs_var | caps: 2000 | ram: 32M
  + binary vfs
  + provides | + service File_system
  + config
    + vfs
      + rump | fs: ext2fs | ram: 16M | writeable: yes
    + default-policy | root: /pkgd | writeable: yes
    + policy | label_prefix: sponge_logdisk -> | root: /log | writeable: yes
  + route
    + service ROM | label_last: ld.lib.so       | + parent
    + service ROM | label_last: vfs.lib.so      | + parent
    + service ROM | label_last: vfs_rump.lib.so | + parent
    + service ROM | label_last: rump.lib.so     | + parent
    + service ROM | label_last: rump_fs.lib.so  | + parent
    + service Block | + child blk_stall
    + any-service
      + parent
      + any-child

#
# sponge_logdisk — the log-path consumer (product component, used
# unmodified, run/sponge-desktop-disk-uefi-usb.run's start node shape).
# tick_log gives headless scenarios a serial marker for the healthy
# state; under the stall its constructor parks on the File_system
# create, so neither "logging to" nor any tick ever appears.
#
# Its own LOG session resolves to core (default-route parent) — the
# product's bootstrap-escape rule shape, simplified because nothing in
# this scenario routes LOG to the sink.
#
+ start sponge_logdisk | caps: 200 | ram: 16M
  + provides | + service LOG
  + config | path: /boot.log | max_bytes: 8388608 | rotate_suffix: .1 | tick_ms: 2000 | tick_log: yes
    + vfs
      + fs | name: log
  + route
    + service LOG | + parent
    + service ROM | label_last: ld.lib.so     | + parent
    + service ROM | label_last: vfs.lib.so    | + parent
    + service ROM | label_last: vfs_rump.lib.so | + parent
    + service ROM | label_last: rump.lib.so   | + parent
    + service ROM | label_last: rump_fs.lib.so | + parent
    + service File_system | + child vfs_var
    + service Timer | + child timer
    + any-service
      + parent
      + any-child

#
# provider_isolation_probe — the per-path checks (bounded; see
# repos/sponge/src/test/provider_isolation_probe/main.cc). Its <vfs>
# node is the pkgd-store consumer shape (run/sponge-pkg-persist.run:
# <vfs><dir store><fs/></vfs> mounts the P4 store region at /store).
#
+ start provider_isolation_probe | caps: 200 | ram: 16M
  + config
    + vfs
      + dir store | + fs
  + route
    + service ROM | label_last: ld.lib.so | + parent
    + service ROM | label_last: sys_marker | + child rom_sys
    + service File_system | + child vfs_var
    + service Timer | + child timer
    + any-service
      + parent
      + any-child

#
# partition_check — the media-alive witness (existing probe,
# repos/sponge/src/test/partition_check): byte-asserts part_block's
# partitions report still lists number="3". Run-script contract per its
# README.
#
+ start partition_check | caps: 100 | ram: 4M
  + route
    + service ROM | label: partitions | + child report_rom
    + service ROM | label_last: ld.lib.so | + parent
    + any-service
      + parent
      + any-child
-
}

#
# Boot modules: the vfs+rump chain libs are transitive deps of
# lib/vfs_rump and not in build_artifacts, so list them explicitly
# (run/sponge-boot.run / sponge-persist-disk.run idiom). On base-sel4
# boot_dir/sel4 auto-injects ld.lib.so.
#
set boot_modules [build_artifacts]
foreach m { vfs.lib.so vfs_rump.lib.so rump.lib.so rump_fs.lib.so } {
	lappend boot_modules $m
}

build_boot_image $boot_modules

# ========================================================================
# Post-build: create P4 (SPONGE-VAR) on the image
# ========================================================================
#
# image/disk produced [run_dir].img with the firmware partitions + P3
# (GENODE) and no free space (it resize2fs -M's P3 and moves the backup
# GPT to the image end). The docs/14 §4.3 grow/repartition sequence
# normally lives in tool/mkdata — which cannot run from inside a Genode
# run script in this environment (logdisk-field-diagnosis §5.4) — so it
# is spelled out inline here, step for step (tool/mkdata.mojo is the
# reference). Idempotent: a re-run finds P4 and skips creation.
#
set img_path "[run_dir].img"
set sgdisk  [installed_command sgdisk]
set e2mkdir [installed_command e2mkdir]

# Parse `sgdisk -i <N> <img>` into {first last}, or {} when absent.
proc part_first_last { sgdisk img num } {
	set info [exec $sgdisk -i $num $img 2>@1]
	if {[regexp {First sector: ([0-9]+)} $info -> first] &&
	    [regexp {Last sector: ([0-9]+)} $info -> last]} {
		return [list $first $last]
	}
	return {}
}

set p4_fresh 0
set p4_existing [part_first_last $sgdisk $img_path 4]

if {[llength $p4_existing] > 0} {
	set p4_info [exec $sgdisk -i 4 $img_path 2>@1]
	if {![regexp {Partition name: '?SPONGE-VAR'?} $p4_info]} {
		puts stderr "sponge-provider-stall: ERROR — P4 exists with an \
unexpected name; refusing to overwrite (reset manually with \
'sgdisk --delete=4 $img_path' if intended)"
		exit 1
	}
	puts "sponge-provider-stall: P4 (SPONGE-VAR) already present — re-run no-op"
} else {
	set p4_fresh 1

	set p3 [part_first_last $sgdisk $img_path 3]
	if {[llength $p3] == 0} {
		puts stderr "sponge-provider-stall: ERROR — P3 (GENODE) not found \
on $img_path (a fresh image/disk output is expected)"
		exit 1
	}
	lassign $p3 p3_first p3_last
	puts "sponge-provider-stall: P3 captured: first=$p3_first last=$p3_last"

	# 1. grow the image file
	exec truncate -s +[expr {$data_mib * 1024 * 1024}] $img_path

	# 2. drop the P3 GPT entry (the bytes stay)
	exec $sgdisk --delete=3 $img_path

	# 3. move the backup GPT to the new end
	exec $sgdisk --move-second-header $img_path

	# 4. re-pin P3 at its old offset + re-apply the name
	exec $sgdisk --new=3:$p3_first:$p3_last $img_path
	exec $sgdisk --change-name=3:GENODE $img_path

	# 5. create P4 in the new free space (BACKUP_GPT_SECTORS = 34:
	#    GPT backup header + partition-entry array + one gap sector,
	#    tool/mkdata.mojo's constant)
	set total_sectors [expr {[file size $img_path] / 512}]
	set p4_first_req  [expr {$p3_last + 1}]
	set p4_last_req   [expr {$total_sectors - 34}]
	if {$p4_last_req <= $p4_first_req} {
		puts stderr "sponge-provider-stall: ERROR — no room for P4 \
(p4_first=$p4_first_req p4_last=$p4_last_req); data-size $data_mib MiB \
too small for this image"
		exit 1
	}
	exec $sgdisk --new=4:$p4_first_req:$p4_last_req $img_path
	exec $sgdisk --change-name=4:SPONGE-VAR $img_path

	# 6. format P4 as ext2 at its ACTUAL byte offset. sgdisk auto-aligns
	#    partition starts to 2048-sector boundaries, so re-query (the
	#    tool/mkdata lesson: formatting at the requested offset would
	#    silently corrupt). mke2fs's own exit status is NOT the success
	#    signal in this environment (logdisk-field-diagnosis §5.3) — the
	#    e2mkdir below is.
	set p4 [part_first_last $sgdisk $img_path 4]
	lassign $p4 p4_first p4_last
	set p4_byte_off [expr {$p4_first * 512}]
	set p4_kib [expr {($p4_last - $p4_first + 1) * 512 / 1024}]
	puts "sponge-provider-stall: formatting P4 ext2: offset=$p4_byte_off \
size=$p4_kib KiB label=SPONGE-VAR"
	set mkfs [installed_command mkfs.ext2]
	catch {
		exec $mkfs -E offset=$p4_byte_off -L SPONGE-VAR -F -q \
			$img_path ${p4_kib}K 2>@1
	} mkfs_out

	# 7. rebuild the hybrid MBR from the first three GPT partitions
	#    (P4 stays GPT-only — docs/14 §4.3)
	exec $sgdisk --hybrid $img_path
}

# --- stage the P4 directory skeleton (e2mkdir via dd extract/write-back)
#
# /pkgd + /pkgd/store = the package-store region; /log = the log-sink
# region. All must pre-exist: vfs resolves a session root at session
# creation time (logdisk-field-diagnosis §3(c)).
#
set p4 [part_first_last $sgdisk $img_path 4]
lassign $p4 p4_first p4_last
set p4_count [expr {$p4_last - $p4_first + 1}]
set p4_extract "[run_dir].p4_staging.ext2"
exec dd if=$img_path of=$p4_extract bs=512 skip=$p4_first count=$p4_count 2>/dev/null

if {$p4_fresh} {
	# On a fresh P4 this e2mkdir IS the mkfs success signal (§5.3).
	if {[catch { exec $e2mkdir $p4_extract:/pkgd 2>@1 } e2err]} {
		puts stderr "sponge-provider-stall: ERROR — P4 staging failed \
(mkfs did not produce a usable ext2?): $e2err"
		exit 1
	}
} else {
	catch { exec $e2mkdir $p4_extract:/pkgd 2>@1 }
}
catch { exec $e2mkdir $p4_extract:/pkgd/store 2>@1 }
catch { exec $e2mkdir $p4_extract:/log 2>@1 }

exec dd if=$p4_extract of=$img_path bs=512 seek=$p4_first conv=notrunc 2>/dev/null
exec rm -f $p4_extract

puts "sponge-provider-stall: P4 staged: /pkgd, /pkgd/store, /log \
(sectors $p4_first..$p4_last)"

#
# Helper: extract P4 from the image and read a file via e2cp (the
# sponge-persist-disk.run read-back idiom — host-side corroboration,
# independent of any guest log). Returns "" when absent.
#
proc read_p4_file { path } {
	global img_path p4_first p4_count
	set tmp "[run_dir].p4_readback.ext2"
	catch { exec dd if=$img_path of=$tmp bs=512 skip=$p4_first count=$p4_count 2>/dev/null }
	if {![file exists $tmp]} { return "" }
	set data ""
	catch {
		set e2cp [installed_command e2cp]
		set data [exec $e2cp $tmp:$path /dev/stdout 2>/dev/null]
	}
	catch { exec rm -f $tmp }
	return $data
}

#
# QEMU: pin the platform explicitly (Phase 12 W1). Headless; no
# -snapshot so the .img writes are real (single boot anyway — no
# run_power_cycle, logdisk-field-diagnosis §5.2).
#
append qemu_args " -machine q35 -cpu Skylake-Client "
append qemu_args " -nographic -m 1G "

# ========================================================================
# Bounded gates + host-side analysis
# ========================================================================

global qemu_spawn_id

set ps_log [run_dir]/provider-stall.log
log_file $ps_log

#
# Gate 1 (boots the guest): the injection fired. ep_wedge's default
# mode prints its marker and wedges — without this line the whole run
# is void (positive-control leg 1 is asserted host-side too).
#
run_genode_until {.*ep_wedge: alive.*} 120

# Raise the expect buffer before the gates that depend on it
# (run/sponge-quota-deadlock.run idiom).
match_max -i $qemu_spawn_id 500000

#
# Gate 2: the media enumerated (partition_check reads part_block's
# partitions report and exits). Same-boot gate -> 3-arg form.
#
run_genode_until {.*partition-check: PASS.*} 120 $qemu_spawn_id

#
# Gate 3: the probe's verdict is in (bounded workers, always prints).
#
run_genode_until {.*provider-isolation-probe: DONE.*} 120 $qemu_spawn_id

sleep 2
log_file

set fh [open $ps_log r]
set log_text [read $fh]
close $fh

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Positive control — the fault detector must demonstrably fire, or any
# isolation verdict would be void.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------

if {![regexp {ep_wedge: alive} $log_text]} {
	error "provider-stall-control: FAIL (injection not observed — the \
stall body never wedged, so any isolation result would be void). \
full log: $ps_log"
}

if {[regexp -all {sponge_logdisk: logging to} $log_text] != 0} {
	error "provider-stall-control: FAIL (log consumer unaffected — \
sponge_logdisk reached its File_system despite the injected stall; \
the detector is blind or the fault is not on the log path). \
full log: $ps_log"
}

if {[regexp -all {tick alive} $log_text] != 0} {
	error "provider-stall-control: FAIL (log consumer unaffected — \
sponge_logdisk produced tick lines despite the injected stall). \
full log: $ps_log"
}

if {[regexp -all {bystander: alive} $log_text] < 2} {
	error "provider-stall-control: FAIL (container dead — the liveness \
bystander stopped printing, so per-path results would be void). \
full log: $ps_log"
}

if {![regexp {partition-check: PASS} $log_text]} {
	error "provider-stall-control: FAIL (media dead — part_block did \
not enumerate the partitions; that would be a physical-media failure, \
not the injected software stall). full log: $ps_log"
}

puts "\nprovider-stall-control: PASS — injection observed, log consumer \
degraded as expected, container alive, media healthy (software provider \
stall — NOT a physical media/USB failure)\n"

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Per-path verdicts (explicit per-path RED markers)
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------

if {[regexp {provider-isolation-probe: PASS path=sys-rom} $log_text]} {
	puts "provider-stall: path=sys-rom    PASS \
(rom_sys served from the healthy disk during the stall)"
} else {
	error "provider-stall: path=sys-rom    RED — the unrelated system ROM \
chain did not survive the provider stall (see \
provider-isolation-probe: RED path=sys-rom). full log: $ps_log"
}

if {[regexp {provider-isolation-probe: PASS path=pkgd-store} $log_text]} {

	# ---- GREEN: the P3.2 vfs_pkg/vfs_log split is in place. ----
	# Corroborate the guest claim on media (host-side read-back).
	set store_data [read_p4_file /pkgd/store/pstall.txt]
	if {![regexp {provider-isolation-probe store roundtrip} $store_data]} {
		error "provider-stall: GREEN claim not corroborated on media — \
/pkgd/store/pstall.txt missing or wrong on P4: '$store_data'. \
full log: $ps_log"
	}
	puts "provider-stall: path=pkgd-store PASS \
(store round-trip + media read-back)"
	puts "provider-stall: path=log-sink   DEGRADED (expected — the stall \
stays on the log path, sponge_logdisk never reached its File_system)"
	puts "\nprovider-stall: PASS - the log-path stall stayed on its own \
provider path (the vfs_pkg/vfs_log split holds): system ROM and the \
package store kept working while the log sink degraded\n"

} else {

	# ---- RED: today's shared vfs_var — the store parked with it. ----
	puts "provider-stall: path=pkgd-store RED (shared vfs_var fate — \
the package-store create rode the same provider instance as the \
stalled log path)"
	set store_data [read_p4_file /pkgd/store/pstall.txt]
	if {$store_data ne ""} {
		error "provider-stall: unexpected media state — \
/pkgd/store/pstall.txt exists although the probe reported the create \
parked: '$store_data'. full log: $ps_log"
	}
	puts "provider-stall: path=log-sink   DEGRADED (expected — \
sponge_logdisk's File_system create is parked on the stalled provider)"
	error "provider-stall: RED - today's shared vfs_var gives the \
package store and the log sink ONE provider path: stalling the log \
path stalled the store too (per-path RED markers above; full log: \
$ps_log). The P3.2 vfs_pkg/vfs_log split (see this file's header) \
flips this scenario green."
}
